s kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-frozen-margin"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-frozen-margin"],"id":"long.thm-frozen-margin","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.13 (Equivalent sign and vanishing conditions)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.13, p. 48, label thm:frozen-margin","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For the prefix $D=G\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,k\\}$ define\n$$\nF_k(J)=\\sum_{i=1}^{J}c_D(k+1+i)2^{J-i}-2^J C_D(k).\n$$\nThis is a finite integer expression: it compares the next $J$ divisor counts of the fixed prefix with its centred carry. Let $s_n$ denote the integer greedy remainder at depth $2n$, with weights $q(2n,d)$ for $2\\le d<n$ and target $2^{2n-1}-2^n$. The following conditions each imply $1/2\\in\\mathcal A$:*\n\n1.  *For every skipped rank $n\\ge3$, $F_{n-1}(n)\\ge0$.*\n\n2.  *For every skipped rank $n\\ge3$ at which the real and integer greedy words agree on $\\{2,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, $s_n=0$.*\n\n3.  *For every skipped rank $n\\ge3$, $B(2n)<s_n$.*\n\n*Conditions (i) and (ii) are equivalent. Condition (iii) implies them; no converse or strict separation is established here. These hypotheses must hold at every indicated skipped rank, not merely through a finite computed range.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-frozen-margin","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-frozen-margin","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-frozen-margin%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_of_skippedFullShellNonnegative%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-frozen-margin%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_of_skippedFull